{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
  "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:15 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stephen R. McCallister",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court has always held that the defendant's voluntary statements obtained in violation of constitutional standards may be used for impeachment purposes when the defendant testifies at trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: When does -- when does the Sixth Amendment violation occur?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Would it make no difference, I take it, General McAllister, if this had been a police officer who was pretending to be a cellmate?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the jury acquitted Mr. Ventris of the murder charge"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Nicole A. Saharsky",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SAHARSKY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This Court has consistently allowed the use of voluntary statements obtained in violation of constitutional standards for impeachment purposes, and that same rule should apply here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. SAHARSKY",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the fact that the evidence would be unavailable in the government's case-in-chief really is a strong price that the government pays. And -- and this Court recognized it in in Havens, in Walder, in Harris, in Hass, in Harvey, and in all of those prior cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Saharsky, I am still a little hung up on -- on whether we would be allowing a constitutional violation. General McAllister said that in the Fifth Amendment area we -- we indeed allow -- allow it to be introduced in rebuttal even though that is the actual constitutional violation. Isn't that the case other than in the Miranda situation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. EDGE",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what we are dealing with in the Sixth Amendment case here is a violation of a core enumerated trial right, and this makes it a very different animal from all the other cases that we are talking about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. EDGE",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. EDGE",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It would, Your Honor, inasmuch it would remove any disincentive for the police to obtain this evidence by this manner in the first place."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: You don't dispute that there was a Sixth Amendment violation at the time this statement was taken, do you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: You urged a -- a fall-back, and you said at least that there may -- there should be a determination by the judge that the defendant intentionally testified falsely. And I was wondering how that would operate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stephen R. McAllister",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF STEPHEN R. McALLISTER ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER MR. McALLISTER: Two points by way of rebuttal. The balancing of the interests here is sprinkling water under the bridge even in the Sixth Amendment context. In both Nix versus Williams and Michigan versus Harvey where the Court was dealing with Sixth Amendment interests and the Sixth Amendment right to counsel violations, the bulk of those cases make clear that the question of what exclusionary effect to give a violation is subject to a balancing analysis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Nix v. Williams, the Court said the Sixth Amendment right to counsel -- and I am paraphrasing slightly -- protects against unfairness by assuring an adversary process in which proffered evidence is tested by cross-examination. And it's done in front of a jury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Would that apply equally for statements under oath?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1356",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b094e89ff63a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
